[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=VRC MIDI Transposer
GenericName=MIDI Transposer
{{#if comment}}
Comment={{comment}}
{{/if}}
Exec={{exec}} %F
Icon={{icon}}
StartupWMClass={{exec}}
Terminal=false
Categories=AudioVideo;Audio;Midi;Music;
Keywords=MIDI;transpose;VRChat;OSC;MQTT;piano;
{{#if mime_type}}
MimeType={{mime_type}};
{{/if}}
{{!--
  Handlebars template for the Tauri bundler (bundle.linux.deb.desktopTemplate
  and bundle.linux.rpm.desktopTemplate; the AppImage uses the deb one). This
  comment is not written to the installed file.

  On Linux productName is "vrc-midi-transposer" (src-tauri/tauri.linux.conf.json)
  so that the bundler installs this as vrc-midi-transposer.desktop instead of
  "VRC MIDI Transposer.desktop". The display name is therefore written out
  above rather than taken from the name variable.

  Variables the bundler provides (tauri-bundler 2.10, freedesktop/mod.rs):
  categories, comment, exec, icon, name, mime_type, long_description. There
  is no variable for the file argument, so "%F" is written out: a double-
  clicked .vrcmt arrives as the first argument. mime_type is the list of
  bundle.fileAssociations[].mimeType (application/x-vrcmt), defined by
  de.marcus-universe.vrc-midi-transposer.xml in /usr/share/mime/packages/.
--}}
